<title>GERMANY: German Oct/Jan sugar output up at 4.18 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>German Oct/Jan sugar output up at 4.18 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>German domestic sugar output in the first four months of the 1996/97 (Oct/Sept) season totalled 4.18 million tonnes, compared with 3.81 million in the same period last season, sugar industry association WVZ said on Monday.</p>
<p>WVZ's montly statistics showed January sugar output at 9,662 tonnes versus 4,771 a year earlier.</p>
<p>Domestic sugar sales in January amounted to 230,494 tonnes compared with 219,247 in January 1996.</p>
<p>Stocks at the end of January totalled 2.91 million tonnes versus 2.58 a year earlier.</p>
<p>January sugar imports of 6,167 tonnes were down from 8,005 in 1996 while January exports of 88,530 tonnes compared with 110,771 a year earlier.</p>
<p>Details (in tonnes, white value)-</p>
<p>					Oct/Jan 96/97   Oct/Jan 95/96</p>
<p>    Domestic sugar output     4,179,152	  3,805,422</p>
<p>    Imports			    27,625	     46,870</p>
<p>    Exports			   622,421	    610,377</p>
<p>    Domestic sales		  911,790	    912,017</p>
<p>    Carry-in stocks on Oct 1    239,562	    250,854</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
